eric chloride channels ClC-0</article-title><source>Nature  (Lond)</source><year>1996</year><volume>383</volume><fpage>340</fpage><lpage>343</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8848047</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Middleton</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Pheasant</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Miller</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Homodimeric architecture of a ClC-type chloride ion channel</article-title><source>Nature (Lond)</source><year>1996</year><volume>383</volume><fpage>337</fpage><lpage>340</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8848046</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="other">Miller, C. 1982. Open-state substructure of single chloride channels  from <italic>Torpedo</italic> electroplax. <italic>Phil. Trans. R. Soc. London.</italic> B 299:401&#x02013; 411.</citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pusch</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Knocking on channel's door: the permeating anion acts as the gating charge in ClC-0</article-title><source>J Gen Physiol</source><year>1996</year><volume>108</volume><fpage>233</fpage><lpage>236</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8894973</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pusch</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Ludewig</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Jentsch</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Temperature dependence of fast and slow gating relaxations of ClC-0 chloride channels</article-title><source>J Gen Physiol</source><year>1997</year><volume>109</volume><fpage>105</fpage><lpage>116</lpage><pub-id pub-id-t